  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The lead they held in the third unraveled in the fourth, and they never found their way back.",
    "what_this_means": "Cincinnati scored three in the fourth to flip a one-run deficit into a three-run lead. That was the game. The Yankees managed a solo home run from Rice but did nothing else. Ten strikeouts, one run, six hits left stranded. They had chances early. Runners on in the first and fourth. They converted zero of six RISP situations. The bullpen held after Rodr\u00edguez exited in the fourth. Hill, Blackburn, Headrick, Cruz, and Doval combining for 4.1 scoreless innings. That competence mattered. It wasn't enough. This is what happens when the offense leaves runners on base and never gets another chance to fix it.",
